      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).\n\n1. Start with the function:\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n\n2. To find the inverse, solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   Add 8 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. Now, replace \\( y \\) with \\( x \\) to express the inverse function:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. We need to find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. To clear the fraction, multiply both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Distribute the 3 on the left side:\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n\n6. Subtract \\( x \\) from both sides to isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   9x - x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   8x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n\n7. Add 24 to both sides to further isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n\n8. Divide both sides by 8:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
