      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that $f(x) = 3x - 8$, we want to find the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$.\n\nStep 1: Replace $f(x)$ with $y$, so we have $y = 3x - 8$.\n\nStep 2: Solve for $x$ in terms of $y$:\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{y + 8}{3} = x\n   \\]\n\nStep 3: Replace $x$ with $f^{-1}(y)$, resulting in:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(y) = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\nStep 4: To find $f^{-1}(x)$, replace $y$ with $x$:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\nStep 5: To solve for $x$ in $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$, we set both expressions equal to each other:\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\nStep 6: Multiply both sides by 3 to eliminate the fraction:\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n\nStep 7: Move all terms involving $x$ to the left-hand side and constants to the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   9x - x = 24 + 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n\nStep 8: Divide both sides by 8 to solve for $x$:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{32}{8}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ for which $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$ is $\\boxed{4}$.",
