      "text": "First, we start by finding $f^{-1}(x)$. The equation for $f^{-1}$ is:\n\\begin{align*}\nf(x) &= y \\\\\n3x - 8 &= y\n\\end{align*}\n\nSolving for $x$ in terms of $y$:\n\\begin{align*}\n3x &= y + 8 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n\\end{align*}\n\nThus, the inverse function of $f(x)$ is:\n\\begin{align*}\nf^{-1}(x) &= \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n\\end{align*}\n\nNext, we are given that $f(x)$ equals the inverse function, so we set $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$. This gives us:\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 8 &= \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n\\end{align*}\n\nTo solve for $x$, we first eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides by $3$:\n\\begin{align*}\n3(3x - 8) &= x + 8 \\\\\n9x - 24 &= x + 8 \\\\\n9x - x &= 8 + 24 \\\\\n8x &= 32 \\\\\nx &= 4\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, for $f(x)=f^{-1}(x)$, the value of $x$ is $\\boxed{4}$. To illustrate this, recall that with $x=4$:\n\\begin{align*}\nf^{-1}(x) &= \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\\\\nf^{-1}(4) &= \\frac{4 + 8}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{12}{3} \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{align*}",
