      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).\n\n1. Start with the function:\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   We want to solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{y + 8}{3} = x\n   \\]\n   So, the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. Next, we need to find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\). This means setting the function equal to its inverse:\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. To eliminate the fraction, multiply every term by 3:\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n\n4. Now, isolate \\( x \\) by subtracting \\( x \\) from both sides:\n   \\[\n   9x - x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n\n5. Next, add 24 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n\n6. Finally, divide both sides by 8:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
